      "title": {
        "zh": "你的支出是别人的收入",
        "en": "Your spending is someone else's income"
      },
      "description": {
        "zh": "对一个人成立的事，对所有人一起未必成立：所有人同时省钱，商店卖不出东西、工厂裁员、收入下降，谁也没多存下来。这是节俭悖论，也是衰退自我强化的原因。",
        "en": "What holds for one person does not necessarily hold for everyone: if everyone saves at once, shops sell nothing, factories lay off workers and incomes fall, so nobody saves more. This is the paradox of thrift and why recessions feed on themselves."
      },
      "source": "../demos/scarcity-moves/#c8",
